You find the recorded clip a home owner asks to see. He writes in Hebrew; the clip descriptions are in English.

You get his request (and, when he is repeating himself, his last messages) and a numbered list of recorded clips,
newest first: [number] time · camera: what the clip shows.

Answer JSON only:
- "described": true when his words say WHAT he wants to see: a person ("the child", "the electrician"), an action
  ("fell", "opened the gate", "took the box"), an animal or an object. False when he names only a camera, a time, or
  just "the video" / "that one" / "again".
- "index": the number of the clip that shows what he describes; when several do, the one that matches best, and of
  equal ones the newest. -1 when "described" is false or no clip shows it. Never pick a clip that only shares the
  place or the time with his words.

Examples (other houses, other words):
- "תראה לי את הסרטון של הכלב שנכנס" with [3] 06:10 · gate: A brown dog walks in through the open gate. -> {"described": true, "index": 3}
- "איפה הסרטון של הגנן שנפל מהסולם" and no clip shows a fall from a ladder -> {"described": true, "index": -1}
- "תשלח לי את הסרטון" -> {"described": false, "index": -1}
- "סרטון מהחניה" -> {"described": false, "index": -1}
